
How to add and push these files from your local machine (exact commands)
1. Clone the repo (if not already):
- git clone https://github.com/Ion-o-koji/khmerVocabularyAzure.git
- cd khmerVocabularyAzure

2. Create the files and commit:
- Use these commands (paste in terminal at repo root):

cat > .nvmrc <<'EOF'
24
EOF

cat > server.js <<'EOF'
const express = require('express');
const path = require('path');
const app = express();

app.use(express.static(path.join(__dirname)));
app.get('*', (req, res) => {
  res.sendFile(path.join(__dirname, 'index.html'));
});

const port = process.env.PORT || 8080;
app.listen(port, () => console.log(`Listening on ${port}`));
EOF

cat > package.json <<'EOF'
{
  "name": "khmer-vocabulary-azure",
  "version": "0.0.1",
  "private": true,
  "engines": {
    "node": ">=24 <25"
  },
  "scripts": {
    "start": "node server.js"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "express": "^4.18.2"
  }
}
EOF

- Then commit and push:
git add .nvmrc server.js package.json
git commit -m "Add Node 24 detection and minimal Express server for App Service"
git push origin main

(If your default branch is named something else, adjust.)

Create an Azure Web App (App Service) and pin Node 24 — CLI steps
(Replace placeholders: <RG>, <LOCATION>, <PLAN>, <APP_NAME>)

1. Login to Azure:
az login

2. Create resource group (if you don't have one):
az group create -n <RG> -l <LOCATION>

Example:
az group create -n khmer-rg -l eastus

3. Create an App Service plan (Linux, B1):
az appservice plan create -n <PLAN> -g <RG> --is-linux --sku B1

Example:
az appservice plan create -n khmer-plan -g khmer-rg --is-linux --sku B1

4. Create the web app with Node 24 runtime:
az webapp create -n <APP_NAME> -g <RG> -p <PLAN> --runtime "NODE|24-lts"

Example:
az webapp create -n khmer-vocab-webapp -g khmer-rg -p khmer-plan --runtime "NODE|24-lts"

5. Ensure Azure uses Node 24 for builds/runtime (explicit app setting):
az webapp config appsettings set --name <APP_NAME> --resource-group <RG> --settings WEBSITE_NODE_DEFAULT_VERSION=24

Deploy options (pick one)

Option A — Deploy via GitHub Actions (recommended)
- Create a repo secret called AZURE_WEBAPP_PUBLISH_PROFILE that contains the publish profile XML you download from the Azure Portal:
  - In Azure Portal: Web App → Overview → Get publish profile → download .PublishSettings file → open it and copy entire contents.
  - GitHub repo: Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → New repository secret → Name: AZURE_WEBAPP_PUBLISH_PROFILE → Value: (paste publish profile)

- Add this GitHub Actions workflow file at .github/workflows/deploy-webapp.yml:

```yaml
name: Deploy to Azure Web App

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main

jobs:
  build-and-deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Setup Node 24
        uses: actions/setup-node@v3
        with:
          node-version: '24'

      - name: Install dependencies
        run: npm ci

      - name: Build (skip if none)
        run: npm run build || echo "no build step"

      - name: Deploy to Azure Web App
        uses: azure/webapps-deploy@v2
        with:
          app-name: <APP_NAME>                # replace
          publish-profile: ${{ secrets.AZURE_WEBAPP_PUBLISH_PROFILE }}
          package: '.'                        # root of repo
